</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Mix- and MoE-DPO provides a unified approach to modular preference alignment. It generalizes DPO with latent expert mixtures, supports efficient variational training, and enables expert reuse, contextual adaptation, and user-specific specialization—advancing the practical and theoretical foundation for aligning LLMs. Beyond the core formulation presented in this paper, the proposed variational framework supports several extensions that broaden its applicability and scalability. These include (i) user-personalized gating, (ii) multi-agent temporal modeling via hidden Markov mixtures, (iii) multimodal alignment through structured group actions, and (iv) scalable training via sparse expert activation and differentiable relaxation (Monte Carlo relaxation of the variational EM). These extensions make Mix- and MoE-DPO well suited for real-world deployment in (i) multi-user, (ii) multi-agent, (iii) multimodal, and (iv) large-scale training settings, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
