</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related Work</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recent extensions have built upon the direct optimization approach of DPO to further improve effectiveness of aligning LLMs with human preferences. Improved robustness and efficiency are achieved with methods that dynamically adjust <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> to handle noisy preference data, or filter low-quality preference pairs to strengthen optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>. The sample-efficient DPO extension of <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-based preference optimization has been proposed to mitigate over-optimization in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite>. Robustness has been further improved by integrating the supervised fine-tuning loss as an implicit adversarial regularizer, or by modifying the underlying preference objective to mitigate overfitting and preference shifts, respectively, in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>, <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>. Additional extensions of DPO include <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The precision and applicability of DPO have also been advanced through targeted extensions. Fine-grained factuality alignment and error reduction in multi-turn dialogues are achieved by optimizing sentence-level preferences and adapting DPO for conversational settings, respectively <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>. Alternative structures—such as reasoning steps or token-level alignment—have been integrated into direct optimization approaches in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>. These contributions collectively enhance DPO’s robustness, efficiency, precision, and applicability in addressing alignment challenges.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Architectural Variants of Mix- and MoE-DPO</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To accommodate diverse deployment scenarios, we consider two primary architectural instantiations of the Mix- and MoE-DPO framework. These variants differ in the degree of parameter sharing among expert policies, balancing expressivity, memory efficiency, and specialization. Both designs are compatible with the core variational formulation in Section <a href="#S2" title="2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and the training algorithm in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Algorithm ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Case 1: Shared Encoder with Expert-Specific Heads</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This parameter-efficient variant builds on a modular architecture in which all experts share a common encoder <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\phi}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\phi}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, parameterized by <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, that produces a joint representation of the input–output pair. Each expert <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is defined by a head-specific transformation <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\psi_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\psi_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math> producing logits for the conditional distribution:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}(y\mid x)=\text{softmax}(h_{\psi_{k}}(f_{\phi}(x,y)))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>ϕ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}(y\mid x)=\text{softmax}(h_{\psi_{k}}(f_{\phi}(x,y))).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The mixture policy is given by the gating-weighted average:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(y\mid x)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\cdot\pi_{k}(y\mid x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(y\mid x)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\cdot\pi_{k}(y\mid x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where the gating weights <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{k}(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{k}(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math> form a probability simplex over experts, as in (<a href="#S2.E1" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). KL regularization is applied using a shared reference policy <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}=\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}=\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> for all experts, consistent with (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This design offers favorable memory and compute scaling by replacing <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> independent policies with one shared encoder and <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> lightweight heads. Optimization can proceed jointly over <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\phi,\{\psi_{k}\},\{w_{k}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\phi,\{\psi_{k}\},\{w_{k}\})</annotation></semantics></math>, or in a partially frozen regime where <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed and only the heads and gating parameters are trained:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{MoE-DPO}}(\{\psi_{k}\},\{w_{k}\}\mid\phi)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>MoE-DPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{MoE-DPO}}(\{\psi_{k}\},\{w_{k}\}\mid\phi).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This setup aligns with the multi-head specialization strategy in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experimental Evaluation ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and supports modular adaptation over diverse tasks without duplicating the full backbone.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Case 2: Fully Independent Experts</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this more expressive variant, each expert policy <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> is independently parameterized with its own encoder, decoder, and reward function <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>. The gating function <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> may be fixed (as in Mix-DPO) or learned (as in MoE-DPO), and each expert may have a distinct reference policy <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>. This structure supports heterogeneity in both modeling and supervision, allowing for maximal task-specific adaptation.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The decomposition of the MoE-DPO loss into per-expert objectives, as shown in (<a href="#S2.E11" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), allows for fully decoupled optimization:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{MoE-DPO}}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathcal{L}_{k}^{\text{MBT}}(\pi_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>MoE-DPO</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>MBT</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{MoE-DPO}}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathcal{L}_{k}^{\text{MBT}}(\pi_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">with each <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> updated independently. This independence facilitates training under domain shifts, user-specific feedback distributions, or multi-objective alignment, as explored in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experimental Evaluation ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The associated reward updates and posterior responsibilities follow the closed-form expressions derived in (<a href="#S2.E10" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) and (<a href="#S2.E7" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>), respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Hybrid Architectures and Dynamic Expert Routing</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The generality of Mix- and MoE-DPO supports hybrid configurations that combine shared and independent components. For instance:</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A shared encoder with <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> expert heads (Case 1) may be combined with <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> independently parameterized experts (Case 2), allowing coarse-grained specialization through routing.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A mixture-of-mixtures architecture can be used in which gating weights distinguish between shared and independent blocks, and the overall policy is a convex combination across both groups.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Personalized or task-conditioned routing can be implemented by conditioning <math id="A2.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> on metadata, enabling efficient multi-user adaptation (cf. Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Mix- and MoE-DPO at Scale ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Such hybrid structures offer favorable trade-offs between parameter reuse and specialization, making them well suited for deployment under memory constraints, on-device adaptation, or transfer learning from expert checkpoints. The modularity of our variational framework ensures compatibility with these extensions, including user-aware gating, sparse activation, and scalable training, as discussed in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Mix- and MoE-DPO at Scale ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> and supported by the convergence analysis in Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Convergence of the Mix- and MoE-DPO Estimation ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{1},\dots,a_{K}\in\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{1},\dots,a_{K}\in\mathbb{R}_{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> be positive real numbers, and let <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\Delta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\Delta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> be any probability distribution over <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Delta_{K}:=\left\{q\in\mathbb{R}^{K}\,\middle|\,q_{k}\geq 0,\ \sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}=1\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.500em">,</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{K}:=\left\{q\in\mathbb{R}^{K}\,\middle|\,q_{k}\geq 0,\ \sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}=1\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then the following identity holds:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}a_{k}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}\log\left(\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)+D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q\,\|\,\frac{a}{\sum_{j}a_{j}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}a_{k}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}\log\left(\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)+D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q\,\|\,\frac{a}{\sum_{j}a_{j}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{a}{\sum_{j}a_{j}}\in\Delta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{a}{\sum_{j}a_{j}}\in\Delta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalized vector with components</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p_{k}:=\frac{a_{k}}{\sum_{j}a_{j}},\quad\text{and}\quad D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q\,\|\,p)=\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\frac{q_{k}}{p_{k}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">and</mtext><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}:=\frac{a_{k}}{\sum_{j}a_{j}},\quad\text{and}\quad D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q\,\|\,p)=\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\frac{q_{k}}{p_{k}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for each <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and fix any <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\Delta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\Delta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the normalized version of <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> as</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}:=\frac{a_{k}}{\sum_{j}a_{j}}\in\Delta_{K}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}:=\frac{a_{k}}{\sum_{j}a_{j}}\in\Delta_{K}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\sum_{k}a_{k}=\log\!\left(\sum_{k}q_{k}\cdot\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sum_{k}a_{k}=\log\!\left(\sum_{k}q_{k}\cdot\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Apply Jensen’s inequality to the concave logarithm function:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\!\left(\sum_{k}q_{k}\cdot\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)\geq\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\left(\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\!\left(\sum_{k}q_{k}\cdot\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)\geq\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\left(\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">with equality if and only if <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}\propto a_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}\propto a_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=p</annotation></semantics></math>. Now rewrite:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\log\sum_{k}a_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\sum_{k}a_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\left(\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)=\sum_{k}q_{k}\left[\log\!\left(\frac{a_{k}}{p_{k}}\cdot\frac{p_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\left(\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)=\sum_{k}q_{k}\left[\log\!\left(\frac{a_{k}}{p_{k}}\cdot\frac{p_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k}q_{k}\left[\log\!\left(\frac{a_{k}}{p_{k}}\right)+\log\!\left(\frac{p_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)\right]=\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\!\left(\frac{a_{k}}{p_{k}}\right)-\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\!\left(\frac{q_{k}}{p_{k}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k}q_{k}\left[\log\!\left(\frac{a_{k}}{p_{k}}\right)+\log\!\left(\frac{p_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)\right]=\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\!\left(\frac{a_{k}}{p_{k}}\right)-\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\!\left(\frac{q_{k}}{p_{k}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\!\left(\frac{a_{k}}{p_{k}}\right)+D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q\,\|\,p)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\!\left(\frac{a_{k}}{p_{k}}\right)+D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q\,\|\,p).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">But <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dfrac{a_{k}}{p_{k}}=\sum_{j}a_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dfrac{a_{k}}{p_{k}}=\sum_{j}a_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the first term becomes</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\!\left(\sum_{j}a_{j}\right)=\log\!\left(\sum_{j}a_{j}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\!\left(\sum_{j}a_{j}\right)=\log\!\left(\sum_{j}a_{j}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}q_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}q_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\sum_{k}a_{k}=\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\left(\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)+D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q\,\|\,p)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\sum_{k}a_{k}=\sum_{k}q_{k}\log\left(\frac{a_{k}}{q_{k}}\right)+D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q\,\|\,p),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (ELBO for the MBT Model). ‣ 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We aim to derive a variational lower bound (ELBO) on the log-likelihood of observing a preference <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y^{+}\succ y^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y^{+}\succ y^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> given a prompt <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, under the Mixture-of-Bradley–Terry (MBT) model.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The marginal likelihood under the MBT model is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)=p(z=k\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)=p(z=k\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the prior mixture weight, and the expert-specific Bradley–Terry likelihood is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-}):=\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-}):=\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> be any variational distribution over the latent expert index <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-}):=q(z=k\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-}):=q(z=k\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\left(\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\left(\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the inequality follows from Jensen’s inequality applied to the concave logarithm function.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">This is the standard form of the evidence lower bound (ELBO), and it can be rewritten as</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\;-\;D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,p(\cdot\mid x)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\;-\;D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,p(\cdot\mid x)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we obtain the lower bound</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\log\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)\geq\mathbb{E}_{z\sim q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})}\!\left[\log\sigma_{z}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\right]-D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,p(z\mid x)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)\geq\mathbb{E}_{z\sim q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})}\!\left[\log\sigma_{z}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\right]-D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,p(z\mid x)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tightness of the bound.</span> The inequality becomes an equality when the variational posterior <math id="A3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> matches the true posterior <math id="A3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>. Using Bayes’ rule, the exact posterior under the MBT model is</p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p(z=k\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p(z=k\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex31.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{p(z=k\mid x)\,\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x,z=k)}{\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{p(z=k\mid x)\,\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x,z=k)}{\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}w_{j}(x)\,\sigma_{j}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}w_{j}(x)\,\sigma_{j}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the bound is tight when</p>
<table id="A3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})=\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}w_{j}(x)\,\sigma_{j}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})=\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}w_{j}(x)\,\sigma_{j}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p7.3" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Equality Decomposition of Reward Mixture). ‣ 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the definition of the mixture reward function from (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r(x,y):=\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\,\exp(r_{k}(x,y))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>log</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y):=\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\,\exp(r_{k}(x,y)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">We apply Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Appendix C Proofs ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> using <math id="A3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}=w_{k}(x)\,\exp(r_{k}(x,y))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}=w_{k}(x)\,\exp(r_{k}(x,y))</annotation></semantics></math> and setting <math id="A3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}=q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}=q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)\left[r_{k}(x,y)+\log w_{k}(x)-\log q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)\left[r_{k}(x,y)+\log w_{k}(x)-\log q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)\log\left(\frac{q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)}{q^{(r)}_{k}(x,y)}\right)\quad\left(\text{recall }q^{(r)}_{k}(x,y)=\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\exp(r_{k}(x,y))}{\sum_{j}w_{j}(x)\,\exp(r_{j}(x,y))}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtext>recall </mtext><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\sum_{k=1}^{K}q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)\log\left(\frac{q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)}{q^{(r)}_{k}(x,y)}\right)\quad\left(\text{recall }q^{(r)}_{k}(x,y)=\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\exp(r_{k}(x,y))}{\sum_{j}w_{j}(x)\,\exp(r_{j}(x,y))}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)\left[r_{k}(x,y)+\log w_{k}(x)-\log q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)\right]+D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q^{(\pi)}\,\|\,q^{(r)}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)\left[r_{k}(x,y)+\log w_{k}(x)-\log q^{(\pi)}_{k}(x,y)\right]+D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q^{(\pi)}\,\|\,q^{(r)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">which matches the decomposition in (<a href="#S2.E8" title="In Theorem 2 (Equality Decomposition of Reward Mixture). ‣ 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r(x,y)=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim q^{(\pi)}(\cdot\mid x,y)}\!\left[r_{z}(x,y)+\log w_{z}(x)-\log q^{(\pi)}_{z}(x,y)\right]+D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q^{(\pi)}\,\|\,q^{(r)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y)=\mathbb{E}_{z\sim q^{(\pi)}(\cdot\mid x,y)}\!\left[r_{z}(x,y)+\log w_{z}(x)-\log q^{(\pi)}_{z}(x,y)\right]+D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q^{(\pi)}\,\|\,q^{(r)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma 3 (MoE-DPO Objective Decomposition). ‣ 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We begin from the MoE-DPO objective in (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{MoE-DPO}}:=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}\!\left[r(x,y)\right]-\beta\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p}\!\left[w_{k}(x)\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi_{k}(y\mid x)\,\|\,\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y\mid x)\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>MoE-DPO</mtext></msub><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mtext>ref</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{MoE-DPO}}:=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}\!\left[r(x,y)\right]-\beta\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p}\!\left[w_{k}(x)\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi_{k}(y\mid x)\,\|\,\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y\mid x)\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(y\mid x)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\,\pi_{k}(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(y\mid x)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\,\pi_{k}(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> and the soft-mixture reward is defined by (<a href="#S2.E2" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="r(x,y):=\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\,\exp(r_{k}(x,y))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mi>log</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,y):=\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\,\exp(r_{k}(x,y)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Apply Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2 (Equality Decomposition of Reward Mixture). ‣ 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\left[r_{k}(x,y)+\log w_{k}(x)-\log q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\right]+D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q^{(\pi)}\,\|\,q^{(r)}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\left[r_{k}(x,y)+\log w_{k}(x)-\log q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\right]+D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q^{(\pi)}\,\|\,q^{(r)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)=\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}{\pi(y\mid x)},\quad\text{and}\quad\sum_{k}q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)=\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}{\pi(y\mid x)},\quad\text{and}\quad\sum_{k}q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking expectation over <math id="A3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim p</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\sim\pi(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\sim\pi(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}[r(x,y)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}[r(x,y)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}\!\left[q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\left(r_{k}(x,y)+\log w_{k}(x)-\log q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}\!\left[q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\left(r_{k}(x,y)+\log w_{k}(x)-\log q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}\!\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q^{(\pi)}\,\|\,q^{(r)})\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}\!\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}(q^{(\pi)}\,\|\,q^{(r)})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}[r(x,y)]=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}\!\left[q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\left(r_{k}(x,y)+\log w_{k}(x)-\log q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y)\right)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}[r(x,y)]=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}\!\left[q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\left(r_{k}(x,y)+\log w_{k}(x)-\log q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">This motivates defining the corrected reward</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y):=r_{k}(x,y)-\log\left(\frac{q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y)}{w_{k}(x)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y):=r_{k}(x,y)-\log\left(\frac{q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y)}{w_{k}(x)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now use the identity <math id="A3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\,\pi(y\mid x)=w_{k}(x)\,\pi_{k}(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\,\pi(y\mid x)=w_{k}(x)\,\pi_{k}(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}\!\left[q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\,f_{k}(x,y)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}\!\left[w_{k}(x)\,f_{k}(x,y)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}\!\left[q_{k}^{(\pi)}(x,y)\,f_{k}(x,y)\right]=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}\!\left[w_{k}(x)\,f_{k}(x,y)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">for any measurable function <math id="A3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying this to <math id="A3.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}[r(x,y)]=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x,\,y\sim\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}\!\left[w_{k}(x)\,\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi(y\mid x)}[r(x,y)]=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x,\,y\sim\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}\!\left[w_{k}(x)\,\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining with the expert-specific KL penalties in the original objective, we conclude</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\text{MoE-DPO}}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}\!\left[w_{k}(x)\left(\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y\mid x)}\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>MoE-DPO</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mtext>ref</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\text{MoE-DPO}}=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p,\,y\sim\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}\!\left[w_{k}(x)\left(\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)-\beta\log\frac{\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y\mid x)}\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Policy-Reward Equivalence under Mixture Models). ‣ 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We seek the form of the expert policy <math id="A3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes the per-expert objective:</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{k}(\pi_{k})=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p}\!\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}\!\left[\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)\right]-\beta\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi_{k}(\cdot\mid x)\,\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(\cdot\mid x)\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{k}(\pi_{k})=\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p}\!\left[\mathbb{E}_{y\sim\pi_{k}(y\mid x)}\!\left[\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)\right]-\beta\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(\pi_{k}(\cdot\mid x)\,\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(\cdot\mid x)\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is the adjusted reward, and <math id="A3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed reference policy.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">This objective is additive over <math id="A3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, so it suffices to maximize the inner functional pointwise for each <math id="A3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Fix <math id="A3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and define</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(y):=\pi_{k}(y\mid x),\quad\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y):=\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y\mid x),\quad\widetilde{r}(y):=\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(y):=\pi_{k}(y\mid x),\quad\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y):=\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y\mid x),\quad\widetilde{r}(y):=\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">We now solve the constrained optimization problem</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi\in\Delta_{\mathcal{Y}}}\left\{\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi(y)\,\widetilde{r}(y)-\beta\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi(y)\log\frac{\pi(y)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y)}\right\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi\in\Delta_{\mathcal{Y}}}\left\{\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi(y)\,\widetilde{r}(y)-\beta\sum_{y\in\mathcal{Y}}\pi(y)\log\frac{\pi(y)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y)}\right\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">subject to <math id="A3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{y}\pi(y)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{y}\pi(y)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the probability simplex over the discrete output space <math id="A3.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">Introduce a Lagrange multiplier <math id="A3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> for the normalization constraint and define the Lagrangian</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda)=\sum_{y}\pi(y)\,\widetilde{r}(y)-\beta\sum_{y}\pi(y)\log\frac{\pi(y)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y)}-\lambda\left(\sum_{y}\pi(y)-1\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>y</mi></munder><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda)=\sum_{y}\pi(y)\,\widetilde{r}(y)-\beta\sum_{y}\pi(y)\log\frac{\pi(y)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y)}-\lambda\left(\sum_{y}\pi(y)-1\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">Taking derivatives with respect to <math id="A3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(y)</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\pi(y)}=\widetilde{r}(y)-\beta\left(\log\frac{\pi(y)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y)}+1\right)-\lambda." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\pi(y)}=\widetilde{r}(y)-\beta\left(\log\frac{\pi(y)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y)}+1\right)-\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">Setting this to zero yields</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(y)=\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y)\,\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\widetilde{r}(y)-\lambda-\beta\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(y)=\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y)\,\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(\widetilde{r}(y)-\lambda-\beta\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> be the normalizing constant ensuring <math id="A3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{y}\pi(y)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{y}\pi(y)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(y)=\frac{1}{Z}\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y)\,\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\widetilde{r}(y)\right),\quad Z:=\sum_{y^{\prime}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y^{\prime})\,\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\widetilde{r}(y^{\prime})\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(y)=\frac{1}{Z}\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y)\,\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\widetilde{r}(y)\right),\quad Z:=\sum_{y^{\prime}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y^{\prime})\,\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\widetilde{r}(y^{\prime})\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p14.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p14.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the optimal expert policy is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}^{*}(y\mid x)=\frac{1}{Z_{k}(x)}\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y\mid x)\,\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}^{*}(y\mid x)=\frac{1}{Z_{k}(x)}\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y\mid x)\,\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y)\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p14.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p14.6.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k}(x)=\sum_{y^{\prime}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y^{\prime}\mid x)\,\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.337em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k}(x)=\sum_{y^{\prime}}\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y^{\prime}\mid x)\,\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\widetilde{r}_{k}(x,y^{\prime})\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. The solution is unique because the objective is strictly concave in <math id="A3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> (linear term minus KL), and the feasible set <math id="A3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{Y}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{Y}}</annotation></semantics></math> is convex and compact.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof that maximizing the ELBO with respect to <math id="A3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to minimizing (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).</h6>
<div id="A3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">We show that maximizing the ELBO with respect to the gating weights <math id="A3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to minimizing the expected KL divergence between the variational posterior and the gating prior, as given in (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall the ELBO from Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1 (ELBO for the MBT Model). ‣ 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, which for a single preference triplet <math id="A3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)\geq\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\left(\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≥</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)\geq\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\left(\frac{w_{k}(x)\,\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A3.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> is the Bradley–Terry likelihood under expert <math id="A3.p16.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.p16.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> is any variational posterior over the expert index <math id="A3.p16.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">Isolate the part of the ELBO that depends on <math id="A3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.p17.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed (as outputs of the E-step), the only term depending on <math id="A3.p17.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log w_{k}(x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log w_{k}(x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, maximizing the ELBO over <math id="A3.p17.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, subject to <math id="A3.p17.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, is equivalent to solving</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\{w_{k}(x)\}}\ \sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log w_{k}(x)\quad\text{subject to }\sum_{k}w_{k}(x)=1,\ w_{k}(x)\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mmultiscripts><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>subject to </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\{w_{k}(x)\}}\ \sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log w_{k}(x)\quad\text{subject to }\sum_{k}w_{k}(x)=1,\ w_{k}(x)\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">This is equivalent to minimizing</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,w(\cdot\mid x)\right)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\frac{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{w_{k}(x)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,w(\cdot\mid x)\right)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\frac{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{w_{k}(x)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p17.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p17.4.1" class="ltx_text">which attains its minimum when <math id="A3.p17.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)=q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)=q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the expectation over <math id="A3.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> yields the training objective</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\argmin_{w_{k}(x)}\ \mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\frac{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{w_{k}(x)}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.500em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\argmin_{w_{k}(x)}\ \mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\frac{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{w_{k}(x)}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p18.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p18.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is precisely (<a href="#S2.E12" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>). Hence, maximizing the ELBO with respect to <math id="A3.p18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to minimizing the expected KL divergence between the variational posterior and the gating prior.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Stochastic EM Algorithm for Mix- and MoE-DPO</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix details the stochastic Expectation–Maximization (EM) procedure used to train the Mix- and MoE-DPO models. Rather than operating on the full dataset, each iteration of the algorithm is applied to a randomly sampled minibatch, enabling scalable training on large preference datasets. The stochastic EM loop alternates between soft expert assignment (E-step) and parameter optimization (M-step), and comprises the following four stages:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E-step:</span> Posterior-responsibility computation over latent experts using the MBT model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">M-step:</span> Policy update via log-normalized preference gradients.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reward update:</span> Reward recomputation for posterior consistency.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">M-step:</span> Mixture-prior update using minibatch-responsibility averages.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Each step is performed on a minibatch <math id="A4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, where the preference triplets are drawn from the full training dataset <math id="A4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>E-Step: Posterior-Responsibility Computation for Preference Triplets</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compute the posterior responsibilities <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> over the latent expert index <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\{1,\ldots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\{1,\ldots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> for each triplet in the minibatch. These responsibilities are derived from the expert-specific Bradley–Terry likelihoods and the current mixture weights:</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Posterior-Responsibility Computation for the MBT Model</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Rewards <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{r_{k}(x,y^{+}),r_{k}(x,y^{-})\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{r_{k}(x,y^{+}),r_{k}(x,y^{-})\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, mixture weights <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{k}(x)\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{k}(x)\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Posterior probabilities <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\dots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\dots,K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute preference likelihood:

<table id="A4.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{k}\leftarrow\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{k}\leftarrow\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              Compute unnormalized responsibility:

<table id="A4.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{q}_{k}\leftarrow w_{k}(x)\cdot p_{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{q}_{k}\leftarrow w_{k}(x)\cdot p_{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg2.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
            Normalize responsibilities:

<table id="A4.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\leftarrow\sum_{j=1}^{K}\tilde{q}_{j},\quad q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\leftarrow\frac{\tilde{q}_{k}}{Z}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mi>Z</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\leftarrow\sum_{j=1}^{K}\tilde{q}_{j},\quad q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\leftarrow\frac{\tilde{q}_{k}}{Z}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table><span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>M-Step: Policy Update via Log-Space Normalized Gradient</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Expert policies <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are updated by maximizing the componentwise MBT objective using stochastic gradients. The loss for expert <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is derived from the log-normalized likelihood ratio:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{k}=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot\log\left(\frac{A^{+}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\right)\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{k}=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot\log\left(\frac{A^{+}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\right)\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we define</p>
<table id="A4.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)^{\beta}\cdot q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{+})\cdot\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y^{+}\mid x)^{-\beta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mtext>ref</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)^{\beta}\cdot q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{+})\cdot\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y^{+}\mid x)^{-\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A^{-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex66.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{k}(y^{-}\mid x)^{\beta}\cdot q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{-})\cdot\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y^{-}\mid x)^{-\beta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mtext>ref</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{k}(y^{-}\mid x)^{\beta}\cdot q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{-})\cdot\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y^{-}\mid x)^{-\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the inverse temperature.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient derivation.</span> We differentiate <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, the parameters of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex67.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\left[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\left(\frac{A^{+}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\left[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\left(\frac{A^{+}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\left[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot\left(\frac{1}{A^{+}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}A^{+}-\frac{1}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\left(\nabla_{\theta_{k}}A^{+}+\nabla_{\theta_{k}}A^{-}\right)\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\left[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot\left(\frac{1}{A^{+}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}A^{+}-\frac{1}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\left(\nabla_{\theta_{k}}A^{+}+\nabla_{\theta_{k}}A^{-}\right)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Using</p>
<table id="A4.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta_{k}}A^{+}=\beta A^{+}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x),\qquad\nabla_{\theta_{k}}A^{-}=\beta A^{-}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{-}\mid x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta_{k}}A^{+}=\beta A^{+}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x),\qquad\nabla_{\theta_{k}}A^{-}=\beta A^{-}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{-}\mid x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">we substitute into the gradient:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex70.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\beta\,\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})}[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot(\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)-\frac{A^{+}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>β</mi><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\beta\,\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})}[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot(\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)-\frac{A^{+}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{A^{-}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{-}\mid x))]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{A^{-}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{-}\mid x))]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\,\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\left[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot\left(\frac{A^{+}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{-}\mid x)-\frac{A^{-}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\,\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\left[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\cdot\left(\frac{A^{+}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{-}\mid x)-\frac{A^{-}}{A^{+}+A^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stochastic gradient estimator.</span> On a minibatch <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the gradient is approximated as</p>
<table id="A4.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{\nabla}_{\theta_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}^{\text{MBT}}=\frac{\beta}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}q_{k}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})\left[\frac{A_{i}^{+}}{A_{i}^{+}+A_{i}^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{-}\mid x_{i})-\frac{A_{i}^{-}}{A_{i}^{+}+A_{i}^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{+}\mid x_{i})\right]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mo>∇</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>MBT</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{\nabla}_{\theta_{k}}\mathcal{L}_{k}^{\text{MBT}}=\frac{\beta}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}q_{k}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})\left[\frac{A_{i}^{+}}{A_{i}^{+}+A_{i}^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{-}\mid x_{i})-\frac{A_{i}^{-}}{A_{i}^{+}+A_{i}^{-}}\nabla_{\theta_{k}}\log\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{+}\mid x_{i})\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">with</p>
<table id="A4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{i}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{i}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{+}\mid x_{i})^{\beta}\cdot q_{k}^{(r)}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+})\cdot\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y_{i}^{+}\mid x_{i})^{-\beta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mtext>ref</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{+}\mid x_{i})^{\beta}\cdot q_{k}^{(r)}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+})\cdot\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y_{i}^{+}\mid x_{i})^{-\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{i}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{i}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex75.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{-}\mid x_{i})^{\beta}\cdot q_{k}^{(r)}(x_{i},y_{i}^{-})\cdot\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y_{i}^{-}\mid x_{i})^{-\beta}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mtext>ref</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{k}(y_{i}^{-}\mid x_{i})^{\beta}\cdot q_{k}^{(r)}(x_{i},y_{i}^{-})\cdot\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y_{i}^{-}\mid x_{i})^{-\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">This gradient is used to update <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> via standard optimizers such as SGD or Adam.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Reward Update: Reward Recalibration for Posterior Consistency</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rewards <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> are updated to enforce agreement between the reward-induced and policy-induced posteriors, using only the current minibatch:</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> Reward Update for Posterior Reweighting</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Current policy <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, reference policy <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mtext>ref</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math>, responsibilities <math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, mixture weights <math id="alg3.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, temperature <math id="alg3.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Updated reward values <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}(x_{i},y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}(x_{i},y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg3.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in\{y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in\{y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each expert <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1,\dots,K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,\dots,K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each input <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in the minibatch <span id="alg3.l4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
               Compute the partition function:

<table id="A4.Ex76" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{k}(x_{i})=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y_{j}\mid x_{i})\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(r_{k}(x_{i},y_{j})+\log w_{k}(x_{i})-\log q_{k}^{(r)}(x_{i},y_{j})\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mtext>ref</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{k}(x_{i})=\sum_{j=1}^{n}\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y_{j}\mid x_{i})\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\beta}\left(r_{k}(x_{i},y_{j})+\log w_{k}(x_{i})-\log q_{k}^{(r)}(x_{i},y_{j})\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in\{y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in\{y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
                 Update the reward:

<table id="A4.Ex77" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}(x_{i},y_{i})=\beta\cdot\log\!\left(\frac{\pi_{k}(y_{i}\mid x_{i})\,Z_{k}(x_{i})}{\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y_{i}\mid x_{i})}\right)+\log\!\left(\frac{q_{k}^{(r)}(x_{i},y_{i})}{w_{k}(x_{i})}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mtext>ref</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi>log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}(x_{i},y_{i})=\beta\cdot\log\!\left(\frac{\pi_{k}(y_{i}\mid x_{i})\,Z_{k}(x_{i})}{\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}(y_{i}\mid x_{i})}\right)+\log\!\left(\frac{q_{k}^{(r)}(x_{i},y_{i})}{w_{k}(x_{i})}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg3.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>M-Step: Mixture-Prior Update (Batch-wise)</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Mixture priors <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> are updated using the minibatch-specific posterior responsibilities. The update differs between Mix-DPO and MoE-DPO.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Mix-DPO (input-independent weights).</span>
The mixture weights <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}\in\Delta^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}\in\Delta^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> are global parameters. The minibatch update is</p>
<table id="A4.Ex78" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}\leftarrow\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}q_{k}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}\leftarrow\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}q_{k}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the minibatch size. This estimate replaces the full-batch average and reflects the current soft-assignment statistics over the minibatch.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MoE-DPO (input-dependent gating).</span>
The gating function <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)=\text{softmax}(g_{k}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)=\text{softmax}(g_{k}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> is trained by minimizing the minibatch-averaged KL divergence:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex79" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{w_{k}(x)}\ \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})\log\frac{q_{k}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})}{w_{k}(x_{i})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.667em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{w_{k}(x)}\ \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})\log\frac{q_{k}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})}{w_{k}(x_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This corresponds to supervised learning over inputs <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with soft labels <math id="A4.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{q_{k}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q_{k}(x_{i},y_{i}^{+},y_{i}^{-})\}</annotation></semantics></math>, implemented via cross-entropy loss on the gating logits.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Numerical Considerations</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All computations are performed on minibatches to support scalable training. We apply the log-sum-exp trick to evaluate partition functions and normalizers for numerical stability. Gradients are computed via automatic differentiation and optimized with standard stochastic optimizers.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Mix- and MoE-DPO at Scale</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Mix- and MoE-DPO framework supports a range of scalable training regimes, offering flexibility across modeling capacity, inference fidelity, and computational constraints. Depending on the deployment setting, different components of the model can be emphasized or fixed during optimization. For instance, when expert policies <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{k}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> are initialized from strong zero-shot models (e.g., domain-specialized LLMs), they can be held fixed while rewards are computed using the canonical DPO transformation. In such cases, only the gating network, which outputs mixture weights <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{k}(x)\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{k}(x)\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math>, is trained—including for a personalized gating function with user-specific characteristics <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>. This reduces the procedure to updating the gating function via the mixture M-step of a variational EM algorithm, with the E-step used to infer expert-assignment posteriors.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In contrast, the fully end-to-end optimization strategy updates the expert policies, gating network, and reward functions jointly. To support both modular and end-to-end regimes, we introduce two complementary estimation strategies. First, a <span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">regularized variational inference</span> method imposes entropy- and KL-based penalties on the expert-assignment posterior, encouraging confident yet diverse expert selection while preserving a closed-form expression for the variational distribution. Second, a <span id="A5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Monte Carlo relaxation</span> leverages the Gumbel–Softmax reparameterization trick <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite> to enable differentiable sampling over the latent expert index. Both approaches support efficient training with minibatches and eliminate the need for explicit (full-sample) E-step computations in classical EM. The variational strategy stabilizes the E-step by enforcing structure on the posterior, while the Monte Carlo relaxation bypasses it entirely by enabling gradient-based updates through sampled expert assignments. Practitioners can instantiate expert policies as either fixed modules or fully trainable heads, depending on the complexity of the problem, computational resources, and adaptability requirements. Our estimation strategies are compatible with large-scale minibatch training and can scale to billions of parameters without incurring dense-model costs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The framework supports sparse activation, modular reuse, and personalized alignment, making it suitable for deployment in multi-task, multi-user, and resource-constrained settings.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Regularized Variational Responsibilities for the MBT Model</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We extend the Mix- and MoE-DPO framework by introducing a richer regularization structure specifically targeting the MBT posterior distribution <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>. The modified regularized MBT loss is given by:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex80X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex80X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{MBT}}^{\mathrm{reg}}(\{q_{k}\},\{\pi_{k}\},\{w_{k}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>MBT</mi><mi>reg</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{MBT}}^{\mathrm{reg}}(\{q_{k}\},\{\pi_{k}\},\{w_{k}\})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex80X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\Bigg[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\ell_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\Bigg[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\ell_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex80Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex80Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}\,\mathcal{H}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ent</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.684em;" width="0.684em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}\,\mathcal{H}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex80Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex80Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}\,\mathcal{H}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>conf</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.684em;" width="0.684em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}\,\mathcal{H}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex80Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex80Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,\mathrm{Uniform}(\{1,\dots,K\})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>unif</mi></mrow></msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>Uniform</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,\mathrm{Uniform}(\{1,\dots,K\})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex80Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex80Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,w(\cdot\mid x)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,w(\cdot\mid x)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex80Xe"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex80Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w\_global}}\,\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p(x)}\!\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(w(\cdot\mid x)\,\|\,\mathrm{Uniform}(\{1,\dots,K\})\right)\right]\Bigg]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>global</mi></mrow></msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>KL</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>Uniform</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>]</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w\_global}}\,\mathbb{E}_{x\sim p(x)}\!\left[D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(w(\cdot\mid x)\,\|\,\mathrm{Uniform}(\{1,\dots,K\})\right)\right]\Bigg],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the per-component utility is</p>
<table id="A5.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-}):=\log\frac{\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y^{+}\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}\,q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{+})}{\sum_{\eta\in\{y^{+},y^{-}\}}\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(\eta\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(\eta\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}\,q_{k}^{(r)}(x,\eta)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-}):=\log\frac{\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y^{+}\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}\,q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{+})}{\sum_{\eta\in\{y^{+},y^{-}\}}\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(\eta\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(\eta\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}\,q_{k}^{(r)}(x,\eta)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}},\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}},\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}},\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}},\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w\_global}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>unif</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>global</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}},\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}},\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}},\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}},\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w\_global}}</annotation></semantics></math> control the strength of the respective regularizers.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each regularizer acts specifically on <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> with distinct roles at various training phases:</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>: Controls deviation from reference policies <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Active throughout, typically decaying slowly.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}</annotation></semantics></math>: Promotes exploration via high entropy in responsibilities <math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>. Critical early in training.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math>: Drives specialization via low entropy, enforcing confident expert assignments. Crucial in later training phases.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>unif</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}</annotation></semantics></math>: Prevents early collapse onto few experts, regularizing toward uniformity. Emphasized early.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}</annotation></semantics></math>: Aligns posterior responsibilities <math id="A5.I1.i5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> with prior mixture weights <math id="A5.I1.i5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. Useful when priors are informative.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w\_global}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>global</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w\_global}}</annotation></semantics></math>: Regularizes global mixture weights toward uniformity. Strong early, relaxed later.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the extended MBT objective introduces additional regularization terms on the variational posterior, which modify the computation of <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> for each expert. Namely,</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimal Variational Posterior under Regularized MBT Objective)<span id="Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assuming fixed expert policies <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, mixture weights <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{k}(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{k}(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and MBT reward structure <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y)\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimal variational posterior <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes the regularized MBT objective</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{\text{reg}}_{\text{MBT}}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">MBT</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">reg</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}^{\text{reg}}_{\text{MBT}}(q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex82.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\biggl[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\frac{\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y^{+}\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{+})}{\sum_{\eta\in\{y^{+},y^{-}\}}\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(\eta\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(\eta\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,\eta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{k=1}^{K}\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\biggl[q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\log\frac{\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y^{+}\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{+})}{\sum_{\eta\in\{y^{+},y^{-}\}}\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(\eta\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(\eta\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,\eta)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}\,\mathcal{H}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\right)-\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}\,\mathcal{H}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.684em;" width="0.684em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.684em;" width="0.684em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}\,\mathcal{H}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\right)-\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}\,\mathcal{H}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,\mathrm{Uniform}(\{1,\dots,K\})\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>unif</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>Uniform</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,\mathrm{Uniform}(\{1,\dots,K\})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,w(\cdot\mid x)\right)\biggr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>KL</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}\,D_{\mathrm{KL}}\!\left(q(\cdot\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,w(\cdot\mid x)\right)\biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">is given by the normalized distribution</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})=\frac{1}{Z(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\left(w_{k}(x)\right)^{\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}/\alpha}\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\alpha}\log\frac{\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y^{+}\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{+})}{\sum_{\eta\in\{y^{+},y^{-}\}}\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(\eta\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(\eta\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,\eta)}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})=\frac{1}{Z(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\left(w_{k}(x)\right)^{\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}/\alpha}\exp\!\left(\frac{1}{\alpha}\log\frac{\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y^{+}\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{+})}{\sum_{\eta\in\{y^{+},y^{-}\}}\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(\eta\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(\eta\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,\eta)}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where the effective temperature is</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:=\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}-\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>unif</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:=\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}-\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> ensures normalization.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 6 (Optimal Variational Posterior under Regularized MBT Objective). ‣ E.1 Regularized Variational Responsibilities for the MBT Model ‣ Appendix E Mix- and MoE-DPO at Scale ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We maximize the integrand of the regularized MBT objective at each fixed <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the per-component utility as</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-}):=\log\frac{\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y^{+}\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{+})}{\sum_{\eta\in\{y^{+},y^{-}\}}\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(\eta\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(\eta\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,\eta)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>β</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-}):=\log\frac{\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(y^{+}\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(y^{+}\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,y^{+})}{\sum_{\eta\in\{y^{+},y^{-}\}}\left(\dfrac{\pi_{k}(\eta\mid x)}{\pi_{\mathrm{ref}(k)}(\eta\mid x)}\right)^{\beta}q_{k}^{(r)}(x,\eta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Grouping entropy and KL-based regularization terms, introduce</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:=\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}-\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>unif</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:=\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}-\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">The simplified optimization objective becomes</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(q)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}\Big[\ell_{k}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}\log w_{k}(x)-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}\log K-\alpha\log q_{k}\Big]+\text{const}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>unif</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mtext>const</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(q)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}q_{k}\Big[\ell_{k}+\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}\log w_{k}(x)-\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}\log K-\alpha\log q_{k}\Big]+\text{const}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Introducing a Lagrange multiplier <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> for the simplex constraint <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}q_{k}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}q_{k}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, setting derivatives to zero, and exponentiating yields</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})=\frac{1}{Z(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\left(w_{k}(x)\right)^{\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}/\alpha}\exp\!\left(\frac{\ell_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{\alpha}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>α</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})=\frac{1}{Z(x,y^{+},y^{-})}\left(w_{k}(x)\right)^{\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}/\alpha}\exp\!\left(\frac{\ell_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})}{\alpha}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS1.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Normalization ensures <math id="A5.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})=1</annotation></semantics></math>, completing the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">These responsibilities, utilized throughout the EM procedure, reflect a regularized optimization that balances reward alignment with entropy control and KL constraints to priors, specifically the uniform distribution and the mixture weights <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. While the updates of the expert policies <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and the mixture weights <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> maintain their structural form—being explicit functions of these responsibilities—the responsibilities <math id="A5.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> themselves must replace their non-regularized counterparts across all EM algorithm steps. Consequently, this revised formulation preserves the modular decomposition of EM updates but mandates the use of refined, regularized responsibilities in both the M-step policy updates and the estimation of mixture weights.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">For the training strategy, we recommend that (i) only a subset of the regularizers is activated during specific training phases; and (ii) typically, only one entropy-based regularizer (<math id="A5.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A5.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math>) is employed at any given time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">We suggest dynamically adapting the regularization scheme across training phases to achieve a balance between exploration, specialization, and stability:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A5.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Phase</span></td>
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Objective</span></td>
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><span id="A5.SS1.p8.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Active Regularizers</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.SS1.p8.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">Early (Exploration)</td>
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">Maintain diversity, avoid expert collapse</td>
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><math id="A5.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ent</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{ent}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>unif</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_unif}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w\_global}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>global</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w\_global}}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.SS1.p8.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">Middle (Specialization)</td>
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">Encourage confident expert specialization</td>
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><math id="A5.SS1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math>, moderate <math id="A5.SS1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.SS1.p8.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">Late (Stabilization)</td>
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;">Solidify learned specialization, maintain stability</td>
<td id="A5.SS1.p8.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.5pt;padding-bottom:1.5pt;"><math id="A5.SS1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>conf</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{conf}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\mathrm{KL\_w}}</annotation></semantics></math>, low <math id="A5.SS1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">During the early training phase, high-entropy and uniformity regularizers encourage broad expert participation. In the middle phase, confidence-promoting regularizers sharpen the variational responsibilities and encourage expert specialization. In the late phase, regularization terms are adjusted to maintain stability and finalize expert specialization based on learned structures.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Monte Carlo Relaxation for Mixture of Bradley–Terry Estimation</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To eliminate the explicit E-step in the variational EM algorithm for the Mixture of Bradley–Terry (MBT) model, we adopt a Monte Carlo relaxation based on the Gumbel–Softmax reparameterization, which allows replacing hard assignments (e.g., selecting one expert via <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\arg\max" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>max</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\arg\max</annotation></semantics></math>) with soft, differentiable assignments during training. Instead of computing the closed-form posterior responsibilities <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>, we approximate the latent expert assignment <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> by sampling from a continuous relaxation of the categorical distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the unnormalized expert logit scores,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\propto w_{k}(x)\cdot\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})\propto w_{k}(x)\cdot\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and define <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\alpha(x,y^{+},y^{-})\in\mathbb{R}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\alpha(x,y^{+},y^{-})\in\mathbb{R}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> as the vector of logits across components. We draw <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> samples from the Gumbel–Softmax distribution with temperature <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="z^{(l)}\sim\mathrm{GumbelSoftmax}(\log\alpha(x,y^{+},y^{-}),\tau),\quad l=1,\ldots,L," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><mi>GumbelSoftmax</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(l)}\sim\mathrm{GumbelSoftmax}(\log\alpha(x,y^{+},y^{-}),\tau),\quad l=1,\ldots,L,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">i.e.,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{k}=\frac{\exp\!\left((\log w_{k}(x)+g_{k})/\tau\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\!\left((\log w_{j}(x)+g_{j})/\tau\right)},\quad\text{where }g_{k}\sim\mathrm{Gumbel}(0,1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Gumbel</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{k}=\frac{\exp\!\left((\log w_{k}(x)+g_{k})/\tau\right)}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}\exp\!\left((\log w_{j}(x)+g_{j})/\tau\right)},\quad\text{where }g_{k}\sim\mathrm{Gumbel}(0,1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Hence <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(l)}\in\Delta^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(l)}\in\Delta^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the continuous simplex, and these soft assignments act as differentiable surrogates for <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math>. We replace the original MBT loss in (<a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) with a Monte Carlo estimate of the relaxed objective:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex95" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{MC}}=-\frac{1}{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\sum_{k=1}^{K}z_{k}^{(l)}\log\left(\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>MC</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{MC}}=-\frac{1}{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\sum_{k=1}^{K}z_{k}^{(l)}\log\left(\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Expressing the sample <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> as a deterministic, differentiable function of <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and auxiliary random noise <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> enables low-variance gradient estimation through the sampling step.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The KL divergence between the variational posterior and the prior <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{KL}(q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,p(z\mid x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>KL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}(q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\,\|\,p(z\mid x))</annotation></semantics></math> can also be approximated using relaxed samples:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex96" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathrm{KL}}=\frac{1}{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\sum_{k=1}^{K}z_{k}^{(l)}\log\left(\frac{z_{k}^{(l)}}{w_{k}(x)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>KL</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathrm{KL}}=\frac{1}{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\sum_{k=1}^{K}z_{k}^{(l)}\log\left(\frac{z_{k}^{(l)}}{w_{k}(x)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Finally, policy parameters <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, rewards <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, and gating-network weights <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> are updated using these relaxed estimates without requiring a closed-form E-step. This enables fully <span id="A5.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end-to-end</span> training using backpropagation under the Mix- and MoE-DPO frameworks while preserving a variational lower bound on the marginal likelihood.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Compatibility with General Architectures.</span> Monte Carlo relaxation extends seamlessly to architectures where the MoE structure is embedded within transformer layers or other neural architectures, without requiring explicit policy factorization. In such settings:</p>
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Mixture weights <math id="A5.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> are learned via differentiable gating networks.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Expert rewards <math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed via head activations or contrastive objectives.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The relaxed latent variable <math id="A5.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> enables sparse, input-adaptive routing.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">This flexibility makes Monte Carlo relaxation a method of choice in high-capacity deployments, allowing scalable and differentiable training across diverse preference tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Convergence of the Mix- and MoE-DPO Estimation</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report sufficient conditions for the convergence of the Mix- and MoE-DPO estimation procedures under two algorithmically distinct training paradigms:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A6.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A variational EM algorithm with closed-form expert responsibilities, alternating between inference over latent variables and maximization of a variational lower bound <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A Monte Carlo relaxation approach based on the Gumbel–Softmax trick <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, which enables fully differentiable, end-to-end optimization over latent expert assignments.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p3.1" class="ltx_p">While the two methods differ in their treatment of latent variables and optimization flow, they share a unified objective: maximization of a stochastic evidence lower bound (ELBO) under potentially noisy minibatch updates. To this end, we specify a set of shared assumptions on smoothness, boundedness, and variance control that guarantee convergence to stationary points of the ELBO, as detailed in Sections <a href="#A6.SS2" title="F.2 Case 1: Variational EM Algorithm ‣ Appendix F Convergence of the Mix- and MoE-DPO Estimation ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.2</span></a> and <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Case 2: Monte Carlo Relaxation ‣ Appendix F Convergence of the Mix- and MoE-DPO Estimation ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Shared Assumptions and General Conditions</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> denote the model parameters (e.g., expert policies <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, gating weights <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{k}(x)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{k}(x)\}</annotation></semantics></math>), and let <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> denote a (possibly relaxed) ELBO objective.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">General Assumptions for Convergence</span></p>
<ul id="A6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Smoothness)</span> The objective <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuously differentiable in <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, and its gradient <math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz continuous on compact subsets.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Boundedness)</span> The ELBO objective is finite over the admissible domain:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex97" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\infty&lt;\mathcal{L}(\theta)&lt;\infty\quad\text{for all }\theta\in\Theta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\infty&lt;\mathcal{L}(\theta)&lt;\infty\quad\text{for all }\theta\in\Theta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Coercivity)</span> The objective is coercive, i.e.,</p>
<table id="A6.Ex98" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta\|\to\infty\quad\Rightarrow\quad\mathcal{L}(\theta)\to-\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta\|\to\infty\quad\Rightarrow\quad\mathcal{L}(\theta)\to-\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Stochastic Approximation)</span> If gradient updates are computed via stochastic samples, we assume:</p>
<ul id="A6.I2.i4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Robbins–Monro step size conditions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>: <math id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\eta_{t}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\eta_{t}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\eta_{t}^{2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\eta_{t}^{2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unbiased stochastic gradient estimates.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"><span id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">–</span></span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Finite variance of the gradient noise:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex99" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\big\|\widehat{\nabla}_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)-\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)\big\|^{2}\leq C\big(1+\|\theta\|^{2}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mo>∇</mo><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\big\|\widehat{\nabla}_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)-\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(\theta)\big\|^{2}\leq C\big(1+\|\theta\|^{2}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These assumptions are standard in stochastic variational inference and are generally satisfied in the Mix- and MoE-DPO framework under practical architectural and training choices.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Smoothness</span> holds naturally in our model due to the use of softmax parameterizations for policies and gating networks, which are differentiable with Lipschitz-continuous gradients over compact parameter domains. When using Gumbel–Softmax relaxations for latent-variable inference, the objective remains smooth as long as the temperature <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is kept strictly positive during training. Potential violations can occur if gating functions degenerate into hard assignments prematurely (<math id="A6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>), which may introduce sharp, non-smooth transitions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Boundedness</span> of the ELBO is preserved by the finite output space of softmax policies and regularization through KL terms. All terms in the ELBO remain bounded as long as the expert policies do not collapse to delta distributions disjoint from their reference policies. This risk is mitigated through KL regularization and initialization from well-calibrated base models. In practice, numerical instability is avoided by ensuring overlap in support between <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mrow><mtext>ref</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\text{ref}(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>, especially in early training.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Coercivity</span> is enforced by the KL-divergence regularization, which grows superlinearly as the expert policy deviates from its reference. This ensures that unbounded parameter growth leads to penalization in the ELBO. However, coercivity may be weakened if the gating network assigns vanishing weights <math id="A6.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)\approx 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)\approx 0</annotation></semantics></math> to specific experts, effectively nullifying their KL terms. This emphasizes the importance of entropy control in the gating mechanism to prevent expert collapse or neglect.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stochastic Approximation</span> assumptions are supported by minibatch-based training, uniform data sampling, and unbiased reparameterization gradients in the Gumbel–Softmax case. The Robbins–Monro conditions on learning-rate decay are satisfied via standard schedules. Finite gradient variance is generally ensured by using moderate temperatures (<math id="A6.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau&gt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau&gt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>), sufficient samples per minibatch, and normalized reward magnitudes. Variance may increase if reward values are poorly scaled or if the number of latent samples <math id="A6.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is too small in the Monte Carlo setting.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, these assumptions are valid under standard training setups for Mix- and MoE-DPO. Caution is warranted in highly sparse, low-temperature, or degenerate expert-routing regimes, which may require annealing strategies, sample averaging, or additional regularization to maintain convergence guarantees.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Case 1: Variational EM Algorithm</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the variational EM setting, we consider a variational posterior <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\in\Delta^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\in\Delta^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and maximize the ELBO:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex100" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}(q,\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\left[\log p(y^{+},y^{-},z\mid x,\theta)\right]-\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\left[\log q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(q,\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\left[\log p(y^{+},y^{-},z\mid x,\theta)\right]-\mathbb{E}_{q}\!\left[\log q(z\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This objective is optimized alternately via:</p>
<ul id="A6.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E-step:</span> Maximize <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(q,\theta^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(q,\theta^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> while holding <math id="A6.I3.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">M-step:</span> Maximize <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(q^{(t+1)},\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(q^{(t+1)},\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> while holding <math id="A6.I3.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{(t+1)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{(t+1)}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Convergence Theorem (Variational EM).</span> Under the smoothness, boundedness, and coercivity assumptions defined in Section <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Shared Assumptions and General Conditions ‣ Appendix F Convergence of the Mix- and MoE-DPO Estimation ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>, the sequence of variational EM updates satisfies</p>
<table id="A6.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(q^{(t)},\theta^{(t)})\to 0,\quad q^{(t)}\to q^{*},\quad\theta^{(t)}\to\theta^{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(q^{(t)},\theta^{(t)})\to 0,\quad q^{(t)}\to q^{*},\quad\theta^{(t)}\to\theta^{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">i.e., the sequence converges to a stationary point of the ELBO objective. This follows from standard convergence results for coordinate ascent applied to variational EM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">The Mix- and MoE-DPO model is trained by maximizing the marginal likelihood of preference comparisons under a latent-variable mixture model:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\cdot\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>≻</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(y^{+}\succ y^{-}\mid x)=\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\cdot\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the latent variable <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the expert index, <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the input-dependent prior over experts, and <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{k}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{k}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is the reward function for expert <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We consider the variational EM algorithm that maximizes the evidence lower bound (ELBO) for the marginal likelihood of preference observations. Each iteration <math id="A6.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> consists of:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">E-step:<span id="A6.SS2.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Update the variational posterior <math id="A6.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{(t+1)}(z=k\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{(t+1)}(z=k\mid x,y^{+},y^{-})</annotation></semantics></math> using</span></span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q^{(t+1)}_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})=\frac{w_{k}^{(t)}(x)\cdot\dfrac{\exp(r_{k}^{(t)}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}^{(t)}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}^{(t)}(x,y^{-}))}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}w_{j}^{(t)}(x)\cdot\dfrac{\exp(r_{j}^{(t)}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{j}^{(t)}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{j}^{(t)}(x,y^{-}))}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{(t+1)}_{k}(x,y^{+},y^{-})=\frac{w_{k}^{(t)}(x)\cdot\dfrac{\exp(r_{k}^{(t)}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}^{(t)}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}^{(t)}(x,y^{-}))}}{\sum_{j=1}^{K}w_{j}^{(t)}(x)\cdot\dfrac{\exp(r_{j}^{(t)}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{j}^{(t)}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{j}^{(t)}(x,y^{-}))}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">which minimizes the KL divergence to the true posterior and hence increases the ELBO.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">M-step:<span id="A6.SS2.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Perform stochastic gradient ascent on the ELBO:</span></span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{(t+1)}=\theta^{(t)}+\eta_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(q^{(t+1)},\theta^{(t)})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{(t+1)}=\theta^{(t)}+\eta_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(q^{(t+1)},\theta^{(t)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the collection of model parameters, including <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\pi_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\pi_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{w_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{w_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and potentially shared parameters, and <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the Robbins–Monro conditions <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\eta_{t}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\eta_{t}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\eta_{t}^{2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\eta_{t}^{2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1 (Monotonic improvement).<span id="A6.SS2.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The E-step yields a strict increase (or no decrease) in the ELBO due to Jensen’s inequality:</span></span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(q^{(t+1)},\theta^{(t)})\geq\mathcal{L}(q^{(t)},\theta^{(t)})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(q^{(t+1)},\theta^{(t)})\geq\mathcal{L}(q^{(t)},\theta^{(t)}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">The M-step, via stochastic gradient ascent, increases <math id="A6.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(q^{(t+1)},\theta^{(t+1)})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathcal{L}(q^{(t+1)},\theta^{(t+1)})]</annotation></semantics></math> in expectation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2 (Boundedness).<span id="A6.SS2.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
By assumption, <math id="A6.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(q,\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(q,\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded above. Hence, the sequence <math id="A6.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{L}(q^{(t)},\theta^{(t)})\}_{t=1}^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{L}(q^{(t)},\theta^{(t)})\}_{t=1}^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotone increasing and bounded, and therefore converges.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3 (Robbins–Monro convergence).<span id="A6.SS2.p9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Assuming bounded variance of stochastic gradients and that <math id="A6.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is Lipschitz, the standard Robbins–Monro theorem implies</span></span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(q^{(t)},\theta^{(t)})\to 0\quad\text{almost surely}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>almost surely</mtext></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(q^{(t)},\theta^{(t)})\to 0\quad\text{almost surely}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4 (Convergence to a stationary point).<span id="A6.SS2.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Since the ELBO is continuously differentiable in both arguments and <math id="A6.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(q^{(t)},\theta^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(q^{(t)},\theta^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math> converges, we obtain</span></span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q^{(t)}\to q^{*},\quad\theta^{(t)}\to\theta^{*},\quad\text{with}\quad\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(q^{*},\theta^{*})=0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>with</mtext><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q^{(t)}\to q^{*},\quad\theta^{(t)}\to\theta^{*},\quad\text{with}\quad\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}(q^{*},\theta^{*})=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that <math id="A6.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(q^{*},\theta^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(q^{*},\theta^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> is a stationary point of the ELBO objective.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Case 2: Monte Carlo Relaxation</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this formulation, the latent responsibility <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\{1,\dots,K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\{1,\dots,K\}</annotation></semantics></math> is approximated using a soft Gumbel–Softmax sample <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(l)}\in\Delta^{K-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(l)}\in\Delta^{K-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. The training objective becomes</p>
<table id="A6.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\log p(y^{+},y^{-},z^{(l)}\mid x;\theta)-\log p(z^{(l)}\mid x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{L}\sum_{l=1}^{L}\log p(y^{+},y^{-},z^{(l)}\mid x;\theta)-\log p(z^{(l)}\mid x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z^{(l)}\sim\mathrm{GumbelSoftmax}(\log\alpha(x),\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>GumbelSoftmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z^{(l)}\sim\mathrm{GumbelSoftmax}(\log\alpha(x),\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Convergence Theorem (Monte Carlo Relaxation).</span> Under the smoothness, boundedness, coercivity, and stochastic approximation assumptions stated in Section <a href="#A6.SS1" title="F.1 Shared Assumptions and General Conditions ‣ Appendix F Convergence of the Mix- and MoE-DPO Estimation ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.1</span></a>, the iterates <math id="A6.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{(t)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{(t)}</annotation></semantics></math> produced by stochastic gradient ascent satisfy</p>
<table id="A6.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta^{(t)})]\to 0\quad\text{as }t\to\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta^{(t)})]\to 0\quad\text{as }t\to\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This result follows from stochastic approximation theory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite> combined with the reparameterization-gradient method for continuous relaxations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A6.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the ELBO of the MBT-based Mix- and MoE-DPO model:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex110" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\cdot\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))}\right]-\text{KL regularization}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mtext>KL regularization</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y^{+},y^{-})\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}(x)\cdot\frac{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))}{\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{+}))+\exp(r_{k}(x,y^{-}))}\right]-\text{KL regularization}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Due to the latent discrete structure (expert index <math id="A6.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>), we introduce a continuous relaxation via the Gumbel–Softmax (Concrete) distribution to enable reparameterization.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\sim\mathrm{RelaxedCategorical}(\tau,w(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>RelaxedCategorical</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\sim\mathrm{RelaxedCategorical}(\tau,w(x))</annotation></semantics></math> be the reparameterized latent variable, where <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is the temperature, and let <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(z;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(z;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> be the differentiable reparameterization of the ELBO integrand. Then the Monte Carlo estimate of the relaxed ELBO is</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex111" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}f(z^{(m)};\theta),\quad z^{(m)}\sim\mathrm{RelaxedCategorical}(\tau,w(x))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>M</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>z</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>RelaxedCategorical</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta)=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{m=1}^{M}f(z^{(m)};\theta),\quad z^{(m)}\sim\mathrm{RelaxedCategorical}(\tau,w(x)),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">which is an unbiased estimator of the relaxed objective:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex112" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta)]=\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta)]=\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is the temperature-smoothed ELBO that converges to the exact ELBO as <math id="A6.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(i) Unbiased gradient estimate.<span id="A6.SS3.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Using the reparameterization trick, we have</span></span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex113" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta)]=\mathbb{E}[\nabla_{\theta}f(z;\theta)]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta)]=\mathbb{E}[\nabla_{\theta}f(z;\theta)],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">and <math id="A6.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}f(z;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}f(z;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is an unbiased estimator of <math id="A6.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(ii) Robbins–Monro conditions.<span id="A6.SS3.p6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Assume the learning rates <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\eta_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\eta_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\eta_{t}=\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\eta_{t}=\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\eta_{t}^{2}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\eta_{t}^{2}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(iii) Variance control.<span id="A6.SS3.p7.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Suppose that the variance of the stochastic gradient estimator <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta^{(t)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly bounded, and the relaxed objective <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> is continuously differentiable and satisfies the coercivity condition <math id="A6.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\theta\|\to\infty\Rightarrow\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta)\to-\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\theta\|\to\infty\Rightarrow\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta)\to-\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then, by the Robbins–Monro theorem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>]</cite>, the stochastic gradient ascent updates</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex114" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{(t+1)}=\theta^{(t)}+\eta_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta^{(t)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{(t+1)}=\theta^{(t)}+\eta_{t}\nabla_{\theta}\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta^{(t)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">converge to a stationary point of the relaxed objective:</span></p>
<table id="A6.Ex115" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta^{(t)})]=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta^{(t)})\to 0\quad\text{as }t\to\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mtext>as </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}\mathbb{E}[\widehat{\mathcal{L}}(\theta^{(t)})]=\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{L}_{\tau}(\theta^{(t)})\to 0\quad\text{as }t\to\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Extensions</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User Personalization.</span> Our variational framework naturally supports personalized alignment by conditioning the gating function on user metadata <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math>, yielding personalized mixture weights <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}(x,u;\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}(x,u;\phi)</annotation></semantics></math>. This extension enables MoE-DPO to tailor expert allocation to individual user profiles without retraining expert policies. In settings where pretrained or fixed experts are available (e.g., domain-specific LLMs), personalization can be implemented by fine-tuning only the gating network, effectively leveraging modular reuse for scalable deployment. Our multi-task review generation experiment (Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experimental Evaluation ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) demonstrates this capability: even when experts are fixed, prompt-conditioned gating achieves significant improvements on user-specific reward metrics.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scaling and Sparse Activation.</span> Our training objective admits closed-form per-expert updates (Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem4" title="Theorem 4 (Policy-Reward Equivalence under Mixture Models). ‣ 2 Multi-Expert Preference Alignment ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>) and modular decomposition of the ELBO, which makes MoE-DPO compatible with sparse expert activation. At inference time, only the top-<math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> experts (with the highest gating scores) may be activated per input, significantly reducing compute. Empirically, we observe in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Experimental Evaluation ‣ Mix- and MoE-DPO: A Variational Inference Approach to Direct Preference Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> that even with a single routed expert per prompt (oracle routing), alignment quality improves across tasks, suggesting the potential for scalable deployment via sparse MoE architectures. Extensions to dynamic expert growth and token-to-expert allocation can leverage scaling laws developed in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Differentiable Training via Monte Carlo Relaxation.</span> While our method employs a classical variational EM algorithm, we recommend Monte Carlo relaxation for large-scale or continuous-group settings. Discrete expert assignments can be approximated using the Gumbel–Softmax reparameterization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite>, enabling differentiable training without explicit E-steps. For continuous groups, such as Lie group mixtures, exponential-map reparameterization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> supports structured sampling and backpropagation. These techniques facilitate scalable training of MoE-DPO models with integrated routing and multimodal expert structures.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Additional Experiment Details</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We include additional experimental results on Case 2, which employs independent copies of GPT-2 models fine-tuned for particular reward signals. For training, we run Mix-DPO for 3 epochs with a learning rate of <math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, batch size of 64, and the AdamW optimizer. Average test metric values with standard errors are reported in the table below for average- or model-specific inference styles. We note that average results for independent policies outperform the parameter-sharing policy specification of Case 1 and offer comparable results in the test metrics for individual models.</p>
</div>
<section id="A8.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">H.1 </span>Mix-DPO for Multi-Reward Movie Review Generation</h3>

